course: dictionary
lesson: 1669
title: Choir: a group that sings together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A choir is a group of people who sing together. You can count its members, so a school choir might have twenty singers. «It sounds like a little choir.» Here the word means a small group of singers, and the sound of their voices together is what makes it a choir.
explain: A choir often splits into parts. «A choir often splits into parts singing different notes at once, called harmony, so a different note is not always a mistake.» Picture the high voices, the low voices and the middle voices fitting together like layers of a cake.
explain: Use the words around choir to find its meaning. «Many churches sing modern songs with a band; others have choirs and organs.» Churches have choirs, so here a choir is a group that sings. A choir can also mean the part of a church where the singers sit.
fact: A choir is a group of people who sing together.
fact: The choir is also the part of a church where the singers sit.
fact: A school choir practises songs for concerts and assemblies.
fact: You can sing in the choir, join the choir, or go to choir practice.
fact: «Trebles» are the high voices of boys in cathedral choirs, and boys' voices usually drop in the teenage years.
exercise: «Many churches sing modern songs with a band; others have choirs and organs.» In this sentence, what is a choir? | A church bell | A kind of organ with pipes | A band playing loudly | *A group of people who sing together
exercise: «A choir often splits into parts singing different notes at once.» What is this called? | Silence | Echo | *Harmony | Rhythm
exercise: Why does a school choir practise? | To sell cakes at the summer fair | *To get ready for concerts and assemblies | To learn to play the organ only | To stop the teachers from talking
test: «Many boys sing very high before their voices change; cathedral choirs have high voices called trebles.» What are trebles? | A band playing in a church | *The high voices of boys in cathedral choirs | A kind of song sheet | The low voices of grown men
test: Why is a different note in a choir not always a mistake? | Because the singers are lost | Because the choir is too small | Because the church has no organ | *Because the parts sing different notes together, called harmony
exam: Sam says a choir can only be found in a church. What is the best answer? | Yes, every choir sings only in churches | No, because choirs never sing | Yes, because the word only means a church | *No, a school can have a choir that practises for concerts and assemblies
